config LTO_CLANG_THIN
	bool "Clang ThinLTO for vmlinux"
	depends on ARCH_MSM8226 && !FUNCTION_TRACER
	default n
	help
	  Compile the kernel to LLVM bitcode and link vmlinux through one
	  relocatable ThinLTO link in ld.lld. That prelink rebuilds the
	  initcall sections in source link order and applies the genksyms
	  export CRCs; modpost, kallsyms and the final vmlinux link read its
	  native output. The build needs LLVM=1, and Kbuild stops before
	  compiling with any other toolchain.

	  The prelink covers vmlinux alone: the module build stops with an
	  error when any module is selected, and the function tracer, whose
	  mcount records need a native object per compile, stays disabled.

	  If unsure, say N.
